  "term": "meaningful learning",
  "definition": "Meaningful learning is learning that students experience as making sense of what they are doing and helping them engage more deeply with a task. In this source, it is shown in experiences such as structured instruction, collaborative writing, and guided peer feedback that support learners’ development of persuasive essay writing.",
